# Database Conventions

## Migrations

- All migrations live in `supabase/migrations/`
- Name format: `NNN_descriptive_name.sql` (e.g., `001_initial_schema.sql`)
- Never edit existing migrations; always create new ones
- Run migrations locally before deploying: `supabase db push`

## Row Level Security (RLS)

- **Always enable RLS** on tables containing user data
- Policies for public read on reference tables (professionals, availability)
- Policies for user-scoped read/write (consultations, prescriptions, payments)
- Service role bypass for server-side operations via `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`

## Supabase Client Usage

- Backend uses `supabaseAdmin` (service role) in `apps/api/src/lib/supabase/client.ts`
- Client-side Supabase is initialized with `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*` env vars
- Always use prepared statements/parameterized queries (Supabase JS client handles this)
- Use `.select()` with explicit column lists, never `SELECT *`

## Schema Design

- UUID primary keys (`gen_random_uuid()`)
- Timestamps with timezone (`TIMESTAMPTZ`) 
- Enums via CHECK constraints, not Postgres ENUM types
- Foreign keys with appropriate ON DELETE actions
- Composite indexes for common query patterns (e.g., `(patient_id, status)`)
